# WHAT MUST NOT BE PUBLISHED TO abyquotes.com
#
# 2026-08-21. `wrangler.jsonc` sets the static-asset directory to "." -- the whole repo -- so every
# file here was being uploaded and SERVED PUBLICLY. Measured live before this file existed:
#
#   /.dev.vars        200  <- ADMIN_PASSWORD, SESSION_SECRET and INTEGRATION_TOKEN, in the clear
#   /worker.js        200  325KB, the entire server source
#   /.git/config      200
#   /.git/index       200
#   /.git/objects/..  200  <- the whole repository, cloneable, including deleted history
#   /schema.sql       200
#
# This file works like .gitignore and is read by wrangler at deploy time.
#
# RULES FOR EDITING IT:
#   - Adding a pattern REMOVES a file from the public site. Safe direction.
#   - Removing one PUBLISHES that file. Never do it to make something work without checking what
#     else the pattern was holding back.
#   - It only takes effect on `npx wrangler deploy`. Nothing here is enforced by a push.
#
# The real fix is to move the front-end into its own directory and point `assets.directory` at that,
# so the default becomes "publish nothing" instead of "publish everything". This is the urgent stop.

# --- the repository itself -------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.git/**
.githooks
.githooks/**
.gitignore
.assetsignore

# --- secrets and local state -----------------------------------------------------------------
# .dev.vars is wrangler's LOCAL secret file. It is not supposed to leave the machine.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.env
.env.*
.wrangler
.wrangler/**

# --- server code -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# worker.js is the worker ENTRY POINT (`main`), not an asset. It does not need to be downloadable
# and publishing it hands over every admin page, every query and every business rule.
worker.js
worker.js.map
# A GLOB, NOT A FILENAME. wrangler.jsonc was listed here alone, and on 2026-08-23 a new
# wrangler.test.jsonc -- added for the local test harness -- was served publicly with a 200
# until somebody thought to curl it. The deny list must cover the NEXT one of these too.
# The admin guide's SOURCE and its generated page body. Added 2026-08-23 with the guide
# itself, rather than after somebody curled it -- which is how wrangler.test.jsonc was found
# to be public earlier the same day. A NEW ROOT DIRECTORY IS PUBLISHED BY DEFAULT.
# The guide names how ABY decides who to chase; it is reachable ONLY through /admin/guide.
docs
docs/**
wrangler*.jsonc
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules
node_modules/**

# --- build, tooling and data -----------------------------------------------------------------
scripts
scripts/**
schema.sql
agencies.txt
README.md
*.md

# --- the DEAD root-level duplicates ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 2026-08-22. These were left published on 2026-08-21 with the note "work out which are dead and
# remove them deliberately". That has now been done, BY MEASUREMENT rather than by reading:
#
#   - fetched the LIVE https://abyquotes.com/ and listed every src= and href= it emits.
#     It loads assets/css/*, assets/js/*, assets/js/data/*, assets/js/lib/* -- and from the ROOT,
#     exactly one file: save-hook.js.
#   - july-2026.html, the only other page, references NO root-level script or stylesheet at all.
#   - grepped every .html in the repo for a root-relative reference to any of the six. None.
#
# So these six are served to the public and loaded by nothing.
#
# WHY UN-PUBLISH RATHER THAN DELETE: un-publishing is one line and is undone by deleting one line,
# and it closes the exposure now. Deleting them from the repo is a separate, larger decision --
# it also removes the DECOY TRAP, where an edit to a root file changes nothing and reads as "the
# edit did not work" rather than "the edit went somewhere nothing reads" -- and it is left for
# Eric to approve rather than done unattended.
#
# 🔴 save-hook.js IS NOT IN THIS LIST AND MUST NOT BE ADDED. index.html loads it from the root.
# ⚠️ reps.js is PUBLIC BY DESIGN, but the copy the page loads is assets/js/data/reps.js. The ROOT
#    copy is a stale duplicate, so un-publishing it removes an out-of-date rep list, not the tool's.
# 🔴🔴 THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING AND ITS ABSENCE TOOK THE TOOL DOWN.
# .assetsignore is gitignore SYNTAX: a bare `app.js` matches AT ANY DEPTH, so it also matched
# assets/js/app.js, assets/js/data/pricing.js, assets/js/data/reps.js, assets/js/lib/renderer.js,
# assets/js/lib/utils.js and assets/css/quote.css. Deployed 2026-08-22 and every script on the
# public quote tool went 404 -- the page still returned 200 and rendered, which is exactly what
# this kind of outage looks like from the outside. `/app.js` anchors to the ROOT only.
# ⭐ AND IT WAS FOUND IN ONE MINUTE ONLY BECAUSE THE VERIFICATION FETCHED THE ASSETS THE PAGE
# ACTUALLY LOADS, NOT JUST "/" -- a 200 on the page says nothing about the scripts inside it.
/app.js
/pricing.js
/renderer.js
/utils.js
/quote.css
/reps.js

# --- scratch output from the checkers ----------------------------------------------------------
# scripts/check_worker_pages.mjs writes _s_<pageName>_0.js beside the repo root when it extracts a
# page to parse it. They are gitignored, so they never reach GitHub -- but `assets.directory` is
# "." and wrangler uploads the WORKING TREE, so running a checker immediately before a deploy
# would publish them. Measured 404 today; listed so it stays that way by rule and not by luck.
/_s_*.js

# NOTE ON WHAT IS DELIBERATELY STILL PUBLISHED:
#   index.html, july-2026.html, aby-logo.png, save-hook.js and everything under assets/.
#   Those are the tool itself.

# ── SCRATCH AND PROBE FILES ARE NOT PUBLIC ASSETS (2026-08-27) ────────────────────────────────
#
# 🔴🔴 THIS IS NOT HYPOTHETICAL. Testing F-429 wrote four probe files into this directory --
# `.tok.txt`, `.probe.py` and two saved copies of real shared quote pages -- and the very next
# `wrangler deploy` PUBLISHED ALL FOUR. `.tok.txt` held live share tokens. Every one returned
# HTTP 200 on abyquotes.com before they were removed.
#
# ⛔ THE CAUSE IS STRUCTURAL, NOT CARELESSNESS: `assets.directory` is "." -- the REPO ROOT -- so
# anything written beside the code is a public URL the moment somebody deploys. A working file in
# the repo root is the normal thing to do in every other project.
#
# ⚠️ DOTFILES ARE NOT EXEMPT. A leading dot hides a file from `ls`, not from an HTTP GET.
.tok.txt
.probe.py
.p_*.html
*.probe.*
scratch/
tmp/
